{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/542989-beast-and-silent-hill-2","id":542989,"title":"Beast and Silent Hill 2.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-06T14:43:46-07:00","id":542989,"title":"Beast and Silent Hill 2.","content":"Seems a Beast game right off the bat. Pyramid Head is a Soul who hunger is the need to Punish. Silent Hill is it's Lair, and James is stalked by it the entire time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T14:57:26-07:00","id":543055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/542989-beast-and-silent-hill-2#post542989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems a Beast game right off the bat. Pyramid Head is a Soul who hunger is the need to Punish. Silent Hill is it's Lair, and James is stalked by it the entire time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, isn't Pyramid Head a manifestation of part of James's psychology? Would that not make <i>him</i> the Begotten?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:07:30-07:00","id":543088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/542989-beast-and-silent-hill-2?p=543055#post543055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, isn't Pyramid Head a manifestation of part of James's psychology? Would that not make <i>him</i> the Begotten?</div> </div> </div> </div>He is. It's the Homecoming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T20:41:26-07:00","id":543448,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out, and this seems to be confused quite often, that Pyramid heads don't punish the guilty. They were created by James desire to be punished, because he felt like he needed to be punished. Thus pyramid heads do not pass judgement on those that don't believe they need to be punished.<br /> <br /> which is why it made no sense for the silent hill movie to have a pyramid head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T22:01:11-07:00","id":543469,"title":"","content":"It made no sense but it was still awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T15:31:57-07:00","id":544338,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned before that Alessa from the first game fits nicely into being a Beast. Pyramid Head in the game spawn to punish those guilty of murder. Before there was one and then the second appeared after James kills Eddy again later in the game. It does nicely link into a nightmare figure and how it is continually linked with James in the second game. The boss fight where James fights the two Pyramid Heads seems like a fair Homecoming (He even gains a Pyramid Head great knife in the game!).<br /> <br /> I've mentioned about Fog World and Otherworld being Chambers with specific Nightmares enacted in them, respectively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T15:36:38-07:00","id":544341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/542989-beast-and-silent-hill-2?p=543448#post543448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to point out, and this seems to be confused quite often, that Pyramid heads don't punish the guilty. They were created by James desire to be punished, because he felt like he needed to be punished. Thus pyramid heads do not pass judgement on those that don't believe they need to be punished.<br /> <br /> which is why it made no sense for the silent hill movie to have a pyramid head.</div> </div> </div> </div>So pyramid head doesn't punish the guilty, he punishes the <i>guilty</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:03:20-07:00","id":544378,"title":"","content":"What is interesting is that a Pyramid Head does not just target the person they're linked to... The other manifested monsters throughout the setting also get targetted by them. It noticeably seems to target Maria over James too. Though there is a link right there, which I won't speak much on now.<br /> <br /> Interesting is whilst it's earlier sexual motions can be linked to James' specific issues with Mary, the knife wielded by the monster early in the game looks a heck of a lot like the design of <i>Angela's</i> knife... <i>Hm.</i><br /> <br /> Y'know having an ending of the game where James becomes a Pyramid Head would have been amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T03:33:48-07:00","id":544960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/542989-beast-and-silent-hill-2?p=544378#post544378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is interesting is that a Pyramid Head does not just target the person they're linked to... The other manifested monsters throughout the setting also get targetted by them. It noticeably seems to target Maria over James too. Though there is a link right there, which I won't speak much on now.<br /> <br /> Interesting is whilst it's earlier sexual motions can be linked to James' specific issues with Mary, the knife wielded by the monster early in the game looks a heck of a lot like the design of <i>Angela's</i> knife... <i>Hm.</i><br /> <br /> Y'know having an ending of the game where James becomes a Pyramid Head would have been amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that in one of the Other Games? It's not James i think but someone Does Become a Pyramid Head in one of the Endings in one of the Games... I'll have too look it up.<br /> <br /> Edit Homecoming has it....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:43:11-07:00","id":545734,"title":"","content":"Ooh, nice! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I haven't played Homecoming (yet at least), so I didn't really know anything about it. Very nice that the game shares the name with the actual process of becoming a Beast too, nice bonus points there... I really love that. For sure I'm going to make at least one Beast character that takes elements from Silent Hill.<br /> <br /> I'd pick Fog (of course!) and Mirages for initial Lair Traits, though a few more fit as well, mainly Maze, Poor Light and Sealed Exits (broken, rusted locks).<br /> <br /> So if Pyramid Head is a Beast who has the Hunger of Punishment, what character/monster would have the Hunger of Ruin? It is quite probably the one Hunger I'd pass a Beast character (especially one based off the demons from Jacob's Ladder) outside of becoming Jigsaw from Saw when satisfying High Satiety Punishment Hunger. ^__^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T13:52:15-07:00","id":545739,"title":"","content":"Movie Version Alessia would be a Beast with a Hunger for Ruin, Specifically for those of &quot;The Cult&quot; of the Town. She Doesn't want too see them get their &quot;Just&quot; Rewards she wants them and anyone Connected too them Dead, Their Faith Discredited and everyone that follows it Damned. Likely a Tyrant.<br /> <br /> Other then the First game.. I'm not too sure about the characters Etc. Never Really got me as much as it could have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:07:35-07:00","id":545762,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a mix between Punishment and Ruin to me. If she wanted to take over and gain power, or wipe them out to fill the power vacuum, that'd make her a Tyrant.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm fairly interested on someone who feels they need to be punished getting a Homecoming and becoming the enactor of Punishment themselves. There's something a little hypocritical about it, unless the act of being a Beast itself and needing to fulfil the Hunger is torment to the Beast in question. That they want the Soul to stop it's endless thrashing of thirst, but it doesn't and so they must ruin (small r) others lives to silence it. James confronts the Pyramid Head and comes away as it seems like a loss against the Soul to me, that after a clash, the Beast is beaten and so enslaved by the Soul within.<br /> <br /> Now I wonder if such a Beast character would be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:21:46-07:00","id":545784,"title":"","content":"Looks like too get that ending you Have too Not Forgive the Main Characters Parents, thus basically Blaming them and wanting too punish them. (Can't say i blame the Main Character, Being Abused and Treated like a Disowned family member because you've been Marked as a Sacrifice too the Cult)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T14:55:52-07:00","id":545819,"title":"","content":"I just read up you also have to not give the Medipack to Wheeler when you find him stabbed later. I haven't played the game though, so I don't know what interactions that Alex has with this character at any real length.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}